# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository.
#
# Before this file existed, every blob was stored CRLF and nothing enforced it.
# Any tool that wrote LF - rustfmt, an editor, a script - turned a small edit
# into a whole-file rewrite. A single `cargo fmt` produced a diff of +44851
# and -39651 lines across a 47k line codebase, which is unreviewable, and real
# changes were hiding inside that noise.
#
# text=auto means git stores LF and converts on checkout according to the
# platform and core.autocrlf. Line endings therefore stop appearing in diffs
# at all, whatever wrote the file.
* text=auto

# Explicit for the source and data we actually diff.
*.rs      text
*.aur     text
*.toml    text
*.md      text
*.wgsl    text
*.json    text
*.yml     text
*.yaml    text
*.ps1     text
*.sh      text eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these, and never try to diff them as text.
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.gif     binary
*.ico     binary
*.wav     binary
*.mp3     binary
*.ogg     binary
*.ppm     binary
*.glb     binary
*.gltf    binary
*.ttf     binary
*.otf     binary
*.exe     binary
*.dll     binary
*.pdb     binary
*.lib     binary
*.obj     binary
*.aurtape binary
